// Mach-O/ld64 has no overridable alias: __attribute__((alias)) is rejected on
// Darwin, and an assembler `.set` equate produces a non-weak symbol that a hook
// could not override (and would collide with). So `name` is a distinct weak
// symbol whose body is a guaranteed tail call to __imp__##name -- it lowers to a
